Theorem L-4: Partial order reflexive antisymmetric transitive

  Preconditions:
    - a, b, c are AimsState elements per the canonical proof notation
      sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
    - Partial order le is defined as a le b iff join(a, b) = b
      per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-4

  Soundness property:
    Forall a, b, c in AimsState.
      reflexive: a le a
      antisymmetric: (a le b) and (b le a) implies a = b
      transitive: (a le b) and (b le c) implies a le c

  Proof obligation:
    Each axiom follows mechanically from the lattice operations already
    proven sound at L-1, L-2, L-3 + the join-defined order encoding.

    Reflexivity:
      a le a iff join(a, a) = a; the right-hand side is exactly L-3
      (idempotence), already discharged. Witness: cite L-3.

    Antisymmetry:
      Suppose join(a, b) = b AND join(b, a) = a. By L-1 (commutativity),
      join(a, b) = join(b, a), so b = a. Discharge: cite L-1 + the
      definitional unfolding.

    Transitivity:
      Suppose join(a, b) = b AND join(b, c) = c. Compute
      join(a, c) using L-2 (associativity):
        join(a, c) = join(a, join(b, c)) (b le c hyp)
                   = join(join(a, b), c) (L-2)
                   = join(b, c) (a le b hyp)
                   = c (b le c hyp)
      Therefore join(a, c) = c, i.e. a le c. Discharge: cite L-2 +
      stepwise rewriting.

    Componentwise consistency:
      The order le on AimsState is componentwise: a le b iff
      a_d le_d b_d for every dimension d. Per-dimension order
      reflexivity / antisymmetry / transitivity all hold on the
      totally ordered carriers (Access, Consumption, Cardinality,
      Uniqueness, Locality), on the flat Shape lattice (every element
      is comparable only to itself and to Phi), and on the
      componentwise-OR Effect product. Per-dimension finite
      enumeration of the three axioms:
        Access 2 reflexivity + 4 antisymmetry + 8 transitivity
        Consumption 4 + 16 + 64
        Cardinality 3 + 9 + 27
        Uniqueness 3 + 9 + 27
        Locality 5 + 25 + 125
        Shape 5 + 25 + 125
        Effect 8 + 64 + 512

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-dimension finite enumeration discharge per
        section_02::verify_l4_partial_order)
      monotonicity (validates the join-derived order is monotone:
        x le y implies join(x, z) le join(y, z) for any z)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-4 via L-1/L-2/L-3 composition and per-dimension order enumeration
